<H2><FONT COLOR="#D60021">5.6.2.4.</FONT></H2>
</TD>
<TD VALIGN=top>
<H2>Estimate Main and Interaction Effects</H2>
</TD>
</TR >
</TABLE>
</TD>
</TR>



<tr>
<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="15%"><!-- Add marginal notes below --><a NAME="yates"></a><i>Effects
Estimation&nbsp;</i></td>

<td WIDTH="85%"><!-- Add main text below -->Although the effect estimates
were given on the <a href="pri623.htm">dex mean interaction plot</a> on
the previous page, they can also be estimated quantitatively.&nbsp;
<p>Fractional factorial designs with 2 levels can be fit using the Yates
technique, which is described in <a href="../section7/pri7.htm">Box, Hunter,
and Hunter</a>. The Yates technique utilizes the special structure of these
designs to simplify the computation and presentation of the fit. Note that
the center points are not included in the Yates analysis for estimating
the effects.&nbsp;</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td VALIGN=TOP WIDTH="15%"><!-- Add marginal notes below --><i>Dataplot
Output&nbsp;</i></td>

